                        ],
                        "form": "неизбира́тельны"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e6dfe7c4-ce61-363d-8ae2-fe1c4da35dad",
                        "entry_id": "f9aa7d76-57ad-3dea-9b6d-49b8c3dd64ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "не основанный на сознательном выборе; не являющийся выборочным"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "33694bcb-8fb3-4609-9037-25e7f1a059ff",
                                "sense_id": "e6dfe7c4-ce61-363d-8ae2-fe1c4da35dad",
                                "text": "Однако сегодня мы имеем дело с террором неизбирательным, случайным, направленным против почти произвольно выбранных мирных граждан."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e674459e-e9c3-382f-ba2b-a956aa44b54a",
                        "entry_id": "f9aa7d76-57ad-3dea-9b6d-49b8c3dd64ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. поданный против кого-, чего-либо при голосовании, баллотировке"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c4d597c8-349e-4a66-bed4-60f5ddc84946",
                                "sense_id": "e674459e-e9c3-382f-ba2b-a956aa44b54a",
                                "text": "Сказывают, что один купец баллотировался в выборные и почтён был этого звания 6 избирательными шарами против 161 неизбирательного."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "01d0a586-329e-4f66-abe4-23563bb09f82",
                        "source_entry_id": "f9aa7d76-57ad-3dea-9b6d-49b8c3dd64ed",
                        "target_lang_word": "nonselective",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nonselective",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e100d268-364f-3c2d-9825-46b2f7f24680",
                                        "entry_id": "d69c213c-4332-3b49-8260-1ba8f926b86a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not selective"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4dd681a3-02d2-41ba-a0d6-c695866b22f8",
                        "source_entry_id": "f9aa7d76-57ad-3dea-9b6d-49b8c3dd64ed",
                        "target_lang_word": "unselective",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "unselective",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "650a4054-e0d9-3ce4-a05c-083046c19144",
                                        "entry_id": "3c2c0c10-15d9-3a2a-aa38-153472bfd7e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not selective; open and inclusive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee321b2f-1ffc-4f90-9cd3-dd6f7dbd5343",
                                                "sense_id": "650a4054-e0d9-3ce4-a05c-083046c19144",
                                                "text": "The 1851 Exhibition was international and unselective; the 1951 exhibitions, however, will be entirely British."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15c3ee3b-f457-4b93-99ce-d6a94d557eca",
                                                "sense_id": "650a4054-e0d9-3ce4-a05c-083046c19144",
                                                "text": "“I’m preaching the virtues of the unselective small colleges, the ones that are inclusive rather than exclusive,” Mr. Pope said in an interview at his apartment in a retirement community here in the suburbs of northern Virginia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ac59def0-6238-44bc-890e-b81cc856323f",
                        "source_entry_id": "f9aa7d76-57ad-3dea-9b6d-49b8c3dd64ed",
                        "target_lang_word": "indiscriminate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "indiscriminate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2627999-3b75-3695-a925-b8426b5f0b9e",
                                        "entry_id": "fafbff0f-54a3-3c27-890a-01b244219fee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not marked by discrimination or discernment; (by extension) confused, promiscuous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of things"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65cf940f-a11f-4524-9776-e8cccc737e1d",
                                                "sense_id": "c2627999-3b75-3695-a925-b8426b5f0b9e",
                                                "text": "Otanes […] commanded an indiscriminate slaughter, without regard to age or to place."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d663076a-db81-4e29-9ed4-dcfcd61c595b",
                                                "sense_id": "c2627999-3b75-3695-a925-b8426b5f0b9e",
                                                "text": "The UK's fishing industry has complained that Ocean is “indiscriminate” (arguably an ironic adjective for anyone involved in trawling)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6588dd93-dc81-3b8f-b069-ae71585307e3",
                                        "entry_id": "fafbff0f-54a3-3c27-890a-01b244219fee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Without care in making distinctions, thoughtless."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a person"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b210654-9f54-4e6d-95e2-83307f46c4cb",
                                                "sense_id": "6588dd93-dc81-3b8f-b069-ae71585307e3",
                                                "text": "How can anyone be so indiscriminate in making friends as he is?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f9b39cf-5087-46d3-97de-cabed0bf1ac2",
                                                "sense_id": "6588dd93-dc81-3b8f-b069-ae71585307e3",
                                                "text": "An animal so indiscriminate in its eating habits that it eats coal, boat cushions, and tomtoms, would be only too eager to taste a swimmer or a diver—which must look more edible than an unopened can of salmon."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
